.TH NODENAME 4 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
nodename \- the machine's name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/nodename
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /etc/nodename
holds the machine's name on its one line: letters, digits and
.BR \- .
At boot,
.B /etc/sysinit
gives it to the system, and
.B "uname \-n"
then prints it.
.PP
The file is written when the system is installed, by
.BR ifup (1M)
when a line of
.B /etc/inet/interfaces
says
.BI name " host"\fR,
and by the DHCP client's hook when that file says
.B "hostname dhcp"
and the server gives a name.
Each of these also changes the running name at once
.RB ( "uname \-S" ).
To rename the machine by hand, write the new name here (and in this
host's line of
.BR /etc/inet/hosts );
it applies at the next boot, or at once with
.BI "uname \-S " name\fR.
.PP
An update of the base package keeps the file as it is.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/nodename
this file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ifup (1M),
.BR interfaces (4),
.BR uname (1)
